{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01PqnjKBhidsSfefsd1eYKQx", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.nowjakarta.co.id/?p=7568\"}, {\"url\": \"https://journal.unm.ac.id/index.php/PJAHSS/article/download/1584/991/4546\"}, {\"url\": \"https://journal.unm.ac.id/index.php/PJAHSS/article/view/1584\"}, {\"url\": \"https://search.library.wisc.edu/catalog/999810311502121\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.rtbf.be/article/le-ma-nene-ce-rituel-dans-lequel-un-peuple-indonesien-deterre-ses-morts-et-les-rhabille-11049932\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.imago-images.com/en/collections/stock/559744/imago-cultures-of-the-world-toraja-people-in-indonesia\"}, {\"url\": \"https://blog.wego.com/tana-toraja-tradition/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://jurnal.untirta.ac.id/index.php/JPKS/article/download/11268/7408\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.imago-images.de/de/collections/stock/559744/imago-cultures-of-the-world-toraja-volk-in-indonesien\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:17:05.921Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Ma'bua dance Toraja held once every 12 years", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_014rDr9dL7xhbhjwqEtbGjyg", "content": [{"title": "www.nowjakarta.co.id", "url": "https://www.nowjakarta.co.id/?p=7568"}, {"title": "journal.unm.ac.id", "url": "https://journal.unm.ac.id/index.php/PJAHSS/article/download/1584/991/4546"}, {"title": "Revitalization of Moral Values in Pa'Gellu Toraja Culture", "url": "https://journal.unm.ac.id/index.php/PJAHSS/article/view/1584"}, {"title": "Some information is not displayed", "url": "https://search.library.wisc.edu/catalog/999810311502121"}, {"title": "le ma nene ce rituel dans lequel un peuple indonesien deterre ses morts et les rhabille 11049932", "url": "https://www.rtbf.be/article/le-ma-nene-ce-rituel-dans-lequel-un-peuple-indonesien-deterre-ses-morts-et-les-rhabille-11049932"}, {"title": "imago cultures of the world toraja people in indonesia", "url": "https://www.imago-images.com/en/collections/stock/559744/imago-cultures-of-the-world-toraja-people-in-indonesia"}, {"title": "Inside a Remote Highland Culture Where Deceased Family Members Are Kept at Home for Years", "url": "https://blog.wego.com/tana-toraja-tradition/"}, {"title": "untirta.ac.id", "url": "https://jurnal.untirta.ac.id/index.php/JPKS/article/download/11268/7408"}, {"title": "imago cultures of the world toraja volk in indonesien", "url": "https://www.imago-images.de/de/collections/stock/559744/imago-cultures-of-the-world-toraja-volk-in-indonesien"}]}, "The search turned up one source for the 12-year claim, and it is a travel article, so it is thin support.\n\n- **The 12-year cycle:** A Jakarta Now travel article reports a guide describing the Ma'bua as a dance where a priest wears a buffalo head and dances around a sacred tree, and only takes place every 12 years. I found no second source confirming the interval.\n- **What Ma'bua refers to:** An academic article on the Pa'gellu' dance lists ma'bua as the inauguration ceremony of a Tongkonan house, which suggests the name refers to a ceremony rather than only a single dance. That article does not mention a 12-year cycle.\n- **Possible confusion with other rituals:** Other results describe different Toraja rituals with different timing. The Ma'nene, where bodies are cleaned and re-dressed, is held every three years according to one photo caption. Another source says occurring every few years.\n\nOverall, the 12-year figure is plausible but comes from a single secondary travel source. A specialist source on Toraja ma'bua would be needed to confirm it."], "durationSeconds": 6.680628208, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01PqnjKBhidsSfefsd1eYKQx", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
